  "id": "COMPOUND:307 - PROTEIN:4951",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which gefitinib may interact with HL-60 cells, a human promyelocytic leukemia cell line. Gefitinib is reported to target multiple entities, including Transmembrane glycoprotein NMB, IL13 protein, and Myosin-IIIa, all of which are subsequently targeted by flavopiridol. Flavopiridol, a known inhibitor of the proteasome, is implicated in the suppression of HL-60 cells, indicating a possible role in the pathogenesis of these cells. The shared pathway involving flavopiridol suggests that the effect of gefitinib on HL-60 cells may be mediated through the inhibition of a common target, which is then further inhibited by flavopiridol. This integrated pathway highlights a potential mechanism where gefitinib's effects are modulated by flavopiridol, possibly through the disruption of a shared molecular target. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between gefitinib and HL-60 cells, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
